        "For benzene, n=1 gives six pi electrons; its heat of hydrogenation is less exothermic than an isolated-triene model predicts.",
        "Aromatic stabilisation explains why substitution is favoured over ordinary alkene-like addition."),
    classEleven("Hydrocarbons: Senior Secondary", "Electrophilic substitution in benzene",
