    classEleven("Gaseous State: Formative", "Boyle Charles Gay-Lussac and Avogadro laws",
        "The empirical gas laws relate pressure, volume, absolute temperature and amount when the other variables are controlled.",
        "PV constant; V/T constant; P/T constant; V/n constant",
        "At constant temperature, compressing a gas from 2.0 L to 1.0 L doubles its pressure.",
        "Temperature must be in kelvin, and each law applies only while its stated variables remain constant."),
    classEleven("Gaseous State: Formative", "Ideal gas equation and gas density",
