        "In a mixture with xO2=0.21 at 100 kPa total pressure, pO2=21 kPa.",
        "For gas collected over water, subtract water vapour pressure to obtain the dry-gas pressure."),
    classEleven("Gaseous State: Formative", "Kinetic molecular theory",
        "Kinetic theory models an ideal gas as tiny particles in random motion with negligible volume and elastic collisions.",
        "average translational kinetic energy per mole = 3RT/2",
        "At the same temperature, hydrogen and oxygen have the same average translational kinetic energy but different average speeds.",
        "Temperature controls average kinetic energy, not equal molecular speeds or an absence of a speed distribution."),
    classEleven("Gaseous State: Formative", "Molecular speeds and kinetic energy",
        "Most-probable, average and root-mean-square speeds rise with temperature and fall with molar mass.",
        "urms=sqrt(3RT/M); uavg=sqrt(8RT/(pi M)); ump=sqrt(2RT/M)",
        "At one temperature, H2 has a root-mean-square speed twice that of He because speed varies as inverse square root of molar mass.",
        "Use molar mass in kg mol-1 with SI R and keep the ordering urms > uavg > ump."),
    classEleven("Gaseous State: Formative", "Real gases and compressibility factor",
